# Tells `wrangler deploy` (Workers Static Assets) what NOT to upload.
# .gitignore controls what git tracks; it has no effect on what wrangler
# publishes, since wrangler just walks the filesystem. Without this file,
# `npx wrangler deploy` with Output Directory "." uploads the entire repo,
# including .git/ — meaning the full commit history of this "private" repo
# becomes fetchable at https://platformops.srivantechnologies.com/.git/...
# That happened once already; this file is what stops it happening again.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING TO THE REPO
# --------------------------------------------
# This is a DENY-list on a deploy that publishes the whole repo directory.
# That means anything new is published BY DEFAULT and stays published until
# someone remembers to come back here. It has already failed once that way:
# .git was excluded from the start, but tools/ never was, so every build
# script, the command corpus and siteconf.py (both Search Console tokens)
# were served to the public web for as long as the Worker has existed —
# `GET /tools/siteconf.py` returned 200 with the file. The deploy log says
# so plainly in hindsight: it lists `+ /tools/build_k8s.py` as an uploaded
# asset on every release.
#
# The real fix is to build into a dist/ directory and deploy only that, so
# publishing is an ALLOW-list and nothing can leak by omission. Until that
# lands, every new top-level file or directory that is not part of the
# rendered site has to be added below, by hand, or it goes public.

# ── version control / tooling state ─────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.git/**
.wrangler
.wrangler/**
node_modules
node_modules/**
.gitignore

# ── the build system ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every generator, every content data module (cmd_data.py is 51KB of command
# corpus), the page templates, and siteconf.py. None of it is part of the
# rendered site; no page anywhere links into tools/ — checked, the only match
# in 878 pages is an external kubernetes.io URL that happens to contain the
# word "tools". Safe to withhold entirely.
tools
tools/**

# ── belt and braces ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If a source file ever lands outside tools/, catch it anyway rather than
# discovering it on the live site. Plain gitignore-style patterns on purpose —
# these match at any depth and avoid leaning on "**" support in whatever
# wrangler version is installed, since a pattern this file gets wrong fails
# open (publishes) rather than closed.
*.py
*.sh
__pycache__
__pycache__/**
.fontcache
.fontcache/**
